    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25325" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jŭgurtha</span></b> , ae,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
				nephew and successor of Micipsa, king of Numidia, conquered by
				Marius in the war with the Romans;</i> v. <i><span class="en">Sall. J.
			5</span></i> sqq.; <i><span class="en">Flor. 3, 1</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jŭgurthīnus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
				Jugurtha, Jugurthan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conjuratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N.
					D. 3, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bellum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					Epod. 9, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">triumphus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 4, 3, 45</span></i>
			.</div>
